The integration files let PHP's build system invoke Zig to compile an extension.

# [Generate integration files]($heading.id('generate-integration-files'))

Generate the skeleton with `--with-php-build-system` for `config.m4`, `config.w32`, `Makefile.frag` and the module header.

# [Unix shared extensions]($heading.id('unix-shared-extensions'))

In the generated extension directory, run:

```sh
phpize
./configure --enable-my_php_extension
make
```

For `my_php_extension` the default mode is `ReleaseSafe`. Override it with `MY_PHP_EXTENSION_ZIG_FLAGS`.

# [Built-in extensions]($heading.id('built-in-extensions'))

Place the project under `ext/` in the PHP source tree and enable the extension when configuring PHP.

`zig build -Dshared=false` produces the static library. Link it into PHP and enable its module to complete a built-in build. Static archives cannot be loaded through `extension=`.
